{
  "company_name": "MineOps Central",
  "industry": "Mining",
  "use_case": "Mining production monitoring and processing control center",
  "space_title": "MineOps Central - Production Monitoring Control Center 📊",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Mining\n\n**Use case:** Production Monitoring & Processing Control Center\n\nMineOps Central — concentrator plant analytics across 20 processing units spanning primary crushing through grinding (SAG / Ball Mills), flotation, thickening, and material handling. Processing Plant Leads use this space day-to-day to track throughput, recovery, and bottlenecks; Mine Managers and Reliability VPs use it to coordinate mine-to-mill, and CFOs use it to monitor cost per ton, energy intensity, and concentrate revenue exposure.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Mill throughput (tph and tpd) — primary driver of concentrate output; data spans ~100-1000 tph across the plant\n- Plant recovery (%) — target 85-92% for sulfide flotation circuits\n- Concentrate grade (%) — saleable product quality vs. smelter penalty thresholds\n- Equipment utilization (%) — target 85%+ on critical-path mills and crushers\n- Bottleneck count — number of constrained units in the flowsheet\n- Energy intensity (kWh/ton) — opex and ESG-relevant; SAG benchmark 7-10 kWh/t\n- Unplanned downtime hours — direct lost-production impact at $/ton concentrate\n- Plan adherence (%) — actual vs. planned daily throughput\n\n**Data sources**\n- `processing_units` — daily unit records: throughput tph, recovery, energy, status\n- `production_readings` — daily quality readings: ore grade, particle size, moisture, concentrate grade\n- `throughput_snapshots` — weekly planned vs. actual TPD, utilization, downtime, bottleneck flag",
